{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/355751-the-children-of-scions","id":355751,"title":"The Children of Scions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-31T07:50:51-08:00","id":355751,"title":"The Children of Scions","content":"My husband and I are playing a Scion game wherein we want our characters to be married and eventually I can imagine that they will have children together. So would the child of two Scions be a Scion as well? Or would it just be some kind of partially divine creature? Because Ichor has to run through their veins,right? I mean, we're supposed to imagine Ichor is a real thing, not just a euphemism, or at least that's the impression I got, so would a child of 2 Scions be divine? (My character is a Scion of Frigg, my husband's is a Scion of Sun Wukong.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T08:19:39-08:00","id":355765,"title":"","content":"The child of a scion (or two scions) is a <i>potential</i> Scion. No one is a Scion until they have been Visited. There's enough Ichor for the children and grandchildren of Gods to be Visited and made into Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T08:43:39-08:00","id":355773,"title":"","content":"IIRC, if you've become a Scion there's enough Ichor in you to pass down to the next generation. On the other hand, those children you might have count as scions of your divine parent rather than your own, at least until you've reached Divine levels of Legend.<br /> <br /> Whether the child in question takes after the mother or the father, or just whichever deity comes to recognize them first, is something that I don't remember, if it's ever brought up. Given that bands of Scions can very well see romance bloom--and likely either cross-pantheon or at least between the children of two separate gods--it's worth addressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T01:08:45-08:00","id":356423,"title":"","content":"For example: Annabeth Chase (Daughter of Athena) and Percy Jackson (Son of Poseidon). Though I did pose the question of how far down the line someone can be a Scion and I was told that after grandson/daughter, the ichor ceases to be potent enough to stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:47:37-08:00","id":408364,"title":"","content":"So pretty much 4 generations down the line.<br /> <br /> Gods - Children of Gods - Grandchildren of Gods - Great Grandchildren of Gods<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything lower and they're just mortals. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T02:03:35-08:00","id":412569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/355751-the-children-of-scions?p=408364#post408364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So pretty much 4 generations down the line.<br /> <br /> Gods - Children of Gods - Grandchildren of Gods - Great Grandchildren of Gods<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything lower and they're just mortals. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Though they could well be something special via Scion: Origins.<br /> <br /> 7th Son of a 7th Son and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:38:16-08:00","id":412888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/355751-the-children-of-scions?p=412569#post412569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though they could well be something special via Scion: Origins.<br /> <br /> 7th Son of a 7th Son and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe take a cue from Greek myths proper where MOST of the Heroes (especially in the Trojan War) had gods somewhere back in the family tree, but it was largely further back than grandparents. It kinds sucks that Odysseus, Ajax the Greater, etc., etc. are just mere mortals (or super-special-but-not-Hero-special-mere mortals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}